// V3 negative fixture (plans/backlog/FORMAL_VERIFICATION.md task 8).
//
// A verify-mode function whose body uses a construct OUTSIDE the V3
// verifiable subset: a `while` loop (loops + invariants land in V4).
// The verifier must report a precise subset error, not silently skip
// the function and not crash. This fixture needs NO solver — the
// symbolic executor rejects the body before any obligation runs.
//
// V6 task 5 note: the `decreases(n)` measure is what keeps this fn's
// subset failure LOUD — since task 5, a CONTRACT-LESS fn whose walk
// fails the subset degrades to the passing `outside-subset` outcome
// (infrastructure, nothing promised), while a CONTRACTED fn (this one)
// keeps failing. The measure is honest (sum_to terminates) and splices
// no runtime assert.
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

sum_to :: (fn(n : i32, decreases(n)) -> (r : i32))({
  (acc : i32) = i32(0);
  (i : i32) = i32(0);
  while(runtime(i < n), {
    acc = (acc + i);
    i = (i + i32(1));
  });
  acc
});
